SBSAR,"Un fichier SBSAR est un format de fichier compressé utilisé par Substance Designer et d'autres applications Adobe Substance, comme Substance Painter. Il contient des matériaux ou des textures procédurales qui peuvent être ajustés dynamiquement dans les logiciels qui le prennent en charge. Ces fichiers permettent aux utilisateurs de personnaliser les paramètres du matériau, tels que la couleur, la rugosité, le relief, etc., sans avoir à modifier directement la texture elle-même. Le format SBSAR est avantageux pour le développement de jeux et la production de VFX car il permet une grande flexibilité et une personnalisation en temps réel tout en conservant une taille de fichier réduite.",PORTFOLIO%20PART%20V%202024%20Houdini%203D%20&%20Code%20Tech%20Lesso/image%2058.png
Directional Warp,"The ""Directional Warp"" node in Substance Designer distorts an input image based on the direction and intensity specified. This node requires two inputs: the image to be warped and a grayscale image that defines the warp direction and intensity. The intensity of the warp effect can be adjusted, allowing for dynamic and directional texture modifications. This tool is particularly useful for creating effects like wind or water flow on textures, simulating movement or distortion in a controlled direction.",PORTFOLIO%20PART%20V%202024%20Houdini%203D%20&%20Code%20Tech%20Lesso/compressed_clipboard_image%2015.jpg
Levels,"Adjusts the brightness, contrast, and output levels of an input image. Allows for fine-tuning the visual aspects by manipulating the histogram or intensity distribution of the image.",
Blend,"Combines two input images using various blending modes (such as add, subtract, multiply, etc.). This node allows for the creation of complex textures by layering and adjusting the interaction between two source textures.",
Distance,"Computes the distance between points in an image, often used to generate patterns or gradients based on spatial relationships. This can be used for creating bevel effects or simulating shadows and depth in textures.",
Flood Fill,Analyzes an image and separates it into distinct regions based on color or luminance. Each separated area can then be individually manipulated or used as masks for further texturing processes.,
Flood Fill to Gradient,"Takes the regions created by a Flood Fill operation and applies a gradient within those regions. This allows for sophisticated patterns and variations within a texture, by assigning different colors or effects to different parts of the image.",
